  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:2:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "I exhort therefore, that, first of all, supplications, prayers, intercessions, and giving of thanks, be made for all men;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 2:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:2:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:2:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "For kings, and for all that are in authority; that we may lead a quiet and peaceable life in all godliness and honesty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 2:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:2:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:2:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For this is good and acceptable in the sight of God our Saviour;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 2:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:2:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:2:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Who will have all men to be saved, and to come unto the knowledge of the truth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 2:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:2:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:2:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "For there is one God, and one mediator between God and men, the man Christ Jesus;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 2:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:2:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:2:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Who gave himself a ransom for all, to be testified in due time.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 2:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:2:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:2:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Whereunto I am ordained a preacher, and an apostle, (I speak the truth in Christ, and lie not;) a teacher of the Gentiles in faith and verity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 2:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:2:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:2:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "I will therefore that men pray every where, lifting up holy hands, without wrath and doubting.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 2:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:2:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:2:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "In like manner also, that women adorn themselves in modest apparel, with shamefacedness and sobriety; not with broided hair, or gold, or pearls, or costly array;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 2:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:2:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:2:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "But (which becometh women professing godliness) with good works.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 2:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:2:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:2:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Let the woman learn in silence with all subjection.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 2:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:2:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:2:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "But I suffer not a woman to teach, nor to usurp authority over the man, but to be in silence.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 2:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:2:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:2:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "For Adam was first formed, then Eve.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 2:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:2:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:2:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "And Adam was not deceived, but the woman being deceived was in the transgression.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 2:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:2:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:2:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Notwithstanding she shall be saved in childbearing, if they continue in faith and charity and holiness with sobriety.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 2:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:2:15"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
